 "briefing": "# Zepto Briefing: Changes from 16 October to 15 November 2026\n\n## Summary\n\nNo verified changes at Zepto were found for the 30-day window from 16 October to 15 November 2026. Research did not identify any news, product launches, executive or other hires, or deals (partnerships, funding, acquisitions, or other commercial agreements) in that period. Every search returned no results, so this briefing cannot confirm any recent developments. The date range was not extended, and no items outside the window were included.\n\n## Findings by Category\n\n### News\nNo news items dated within the window were verified.\n\n### Product Launches\nNo product or service launches dated within the window were verified.\n\n### Hires\nNo executive or other senior hires dated within the window were verified.\n\n### Deals\nNo partnerships, funding rounds, acquisitions, or other commercial agreements dated within the window were verified.\n\n## Entity Ambiguity\n\nThe research notes identify the target as Kiranakart Technologies, which operates under the Zepto brand. The name \"Zepto\" is also used by other companies in other markets and industries, and the research did not confirm which entity, business unit, or geography the meeting concerns. Background details from earlier messages, including headquarters location, leadership names, and the existence of specific official newsroom or blog pages, were not verified by any search and should not be relied on until checked.\n\n## Gaps and Suggested Verification Before the Meeting\n\nBecause no sources were retrieved, the following should be checked directly before 17 November 2026:\n\n- Zepto's official newsroom and blog, for announcements dated 16 October to 15 November 2026.\n- LinkedIn profiles of Zepto and Kiranakart Technologies leadership, for recent role changes.\n- Regulatory filings for Kiranakart Technologies, including Registrar of Companies records and any SEBI filings, for funding, share allotments, or acquisitions.\n- Major business outlets (for example, Economic Times, Mint, Moneycontrol, Business Standard, Reuters), searched for \"Zepto\" alongside the specific months.\n\n## Open Questions for the Meeting\n\n1. Which Zepto entity, business unit, and geography should this discussion cover, and is that Kiranakart Technologies?\n2. What significant changes in leadership, product, funding, or partnerships has Zepto made since mid-October 2026 that our briefing should reflect?\n3. What are Zepto's priorities for the next two quarters, and which of them would involve external partners or suppliers?\n\n### Sources\n\nNone.",
